WEBVTT

00:00:04.530 --> 00:00:06.470
This is hard.

00:00:08.640 --> 00:00:11.860
What do you want?  You didn't knock!

00:00:11.860 --> 00:00:15.150
Yeager, is he telling the truth?

00:00:15.330 --> 00:00:16.220
"He?"

00:00:16.530 --> 00:00:18.390
Dragan of Team Ragnarok.

00:00:18.680 --> 00:00:23.090
Is it true that you used him as a patsy?

00:00:23.090 --> 00:00:24.320
Patsy?

00:00:25.560 --> 00:00:28.920
I have no clue what you're talking about-

00:00:28.920 --> 00:00:30.550
So it's true?

00:00:31.250 --> 00:00:33.700
Why did you do that?

00:00:33.700 --> 00:00:38.480
I have no clue what you're talking about.

00:00:38.750 --> 00:00:41.180
I see.  You don't remember.

00:00:41.180 --> 00:00:42.300
In that case...

00:00:42.680 --> 00:00:45.030
I'll make you remember!

00:00:45.030 --> 00:00:47.860
I'll talk, so spare my life!

00:00:48.070 --> 00:00:52.320
As you already know, 
Director Godwin needed you.

00:00:52.710 --> 00:00:56.240
He needed a charismatic duelist 
that would do what he wanted.

00:00:56.240 --> 00:00:59.310
A King that couldn't lose.

00:01:00.940 --> 00:01:06.540
Did you really think that you became 
King due to your own abilities?

00:01:06.900 --> 00:01:09.520
I opposed the plan, of course!

00:01:09.520 --> 00:01:12.200
I said that Jack could win without cheating.

00:01:12.200 --> 00:01:15.220
That you wouldn't lose against him...

00:01:19.780 --> 00:01:21.920
I thought he was going to kill me.

00:01:23.980 --> 00:01:28.190
I can't believe that Dragan lost 
on purpose because of Godwin.

00:01:28.310 --> 00:01:32.860
I thought something was up when I saw 
Dragan's face during the exhibition match.

00:01:33.360 --> 00:01:37.130
Jack must be shocked to learn that 
he won because the match was fixed.

00:01:37.320 --> 00:01:40.540
It doesn't matter because Jack didn't know!

00:01:40.540 --> 00:01:41.400
Right, Yusei?

00:01:41.400 --> 00:01:42.220
Yeah.

00:01:42.220 --> 00:01:43.370
Everyone!

00:01:44.100 --> 00:01:45.330
I rented something good!

00:01:45.730 --> 00:01:46.870
What's that?

00:01:47.220 --> 00:01:48.750
Lord of the King!

00:01:48.750 --> 00:01:51.090
It's a movie about Jack becoming the King.

00:01:51.090 --> 00:01:55.830
I rented it because there might be 
footage of his match against Dragan-

00:01:56.860 --> 00:01:57.880
What's wrong?

00:01:57.870 --> 00:01:59.440
It's nothing.

00:01:59.440 --> 00:02:01.960
I see.  Then let's watch.

00:02:08.670 --> 00:02:10.240
Riding Duels.

00:02:10.510 --> 00:02:13.340
These duels evolved in the world of speed.

00:02:13.660 --> 00:02:20.220
The people with the legendary marks who 
risked their lives were known as 5D's.

00:02:35.330 --> 00:02:41.470
Reach out your hand and 
grab a bright tomorrow

00:02:41.710 --> 00:02:51.580
Soar in the infinite skies   BELIEVE IN NEXUS

00:02:52.220 --> 00:02:57.820
No one can stop my wild impulses

00:02:58.190 --> 00:03:03.800
My hand sweats as the battle 
intensifies  This Heart Beat

00:03:04.330 --> 00:03:09.570
I can't avoid this fearsome battle

00:03:09.770 --> 00:03:15.140
I don't want it to end here  Go For It!!

00:03:16.240 --> 00:03:21.510
Stand up  Don't tremble in fear alone

00:03:21.680 --> 00:03:27.320
Remember that you have 
friends waiting for you

00:03:27.550 --> 00:03:33.620
I'm not scared and I'll never give 
up, no matter how powerful the enemy

00:03:33.620 --> 00:03:39.930
With real courage, I'll never lose

00:04:06.320 --> 00:04:12.100
Damaged Pride

00:04:20.180 --> 00:04:22.190
There was only one stipulation.

00:04:23.230 --> 00:04:25.400
That I must not defeat Jack!

00:04:25.400 --> 00:04:28.940
As long as I obey, I'll get 
the money to save my father.

00:04:32.280 --> 00:04:35.890
My father who always supported me!

00:04:44.450 --> 00:04:46.660
I set two cards and end my turn!

00:04:47.800 --> 00:04:55.220
Even if you're the Scandinavian grim reaper, 
you're a powerless sheep against the King!

00:04:56.160 --> 00:04:58.560
I summon Garmr of the Nordic Beasts!

00:05:02.560 --> 00:05:03.950
My turn!

00:05:04.290 --> 00:05:06.910
I summon Power Breaker from my hand!

00:05:10.880 --> 00:05:15.130
Level 4 Top Runner tunes 
Level 4 Power Breaker!

00:05:16.330 --> 00:05:19.070
The pulse of the King now forms a line here!

00:05:19.320 --> 00:05:21.420
Witness the power of the rumbling heavens!

00:05:22.230 --> 00:05:23.800
Synchro Summon!

00:05:24.070 --> 00:05:27.130
My soul!  Red Dragon Archfiend!

00:05:29.880 --> 00:05:33.170
You'll learn about the King's skills!

00:05:33.420 --> 00:05:37.180
Red Dragon Archfiend attacks 
Garmr of the Nordic Beasts!

00:05:37.450 --> 00:05:39.660
Absolute Powerforce!

00:05:42.810 --> 00:05:45.280
Damn!

00:05:46.460 --> 00:05:49.130
2200 points of damage at once!

00:05:49.130 --> 00:05:55.030
With a direct attack on the next turn, the 
King had another overwhelming victory.

00:05:56.260 --> 00:06:01.460
After Garmr of the Nordic Beasts was 
destroyed, Dragan didn't counterattack.

00:06:01.770 --> 00:06:05.940
So the card where Dragan 
lost his pride was...

00:06:06.460 --> 00:06:11.410
The set card that he didn't activate 
when Red Dragon Archfiend attacked.

00:06:11.590 --> 00:06:15.010
I set one card and end my turn!

00:06:15.600 --> 00:06:17.460
I wonder which card it was.

00:06:22.120 --> 00:06:23.040
Jack...

00:06:32.280 --> 00:06:33.230
What's that?

00:06:34.180 --> 00:06:37.160
I just wanted to watch an old movie.

00:06:41.680 --> 00:06:43.910
It's nothing to worry about, Jack.

00:06:44.330 --> 00:06:46.670
Because you didn't know, Jack.

00:06:46.670 --> 00:06:50.500
Besides, that guy wanted money.

00:06:51.750 --> 00:06:53.980
What do you know about the poor!

00:06:55.120 --> 00:06:58.940
How he felt when he accepted 
Yeager's proposal!

00:06:58.940 --> 00:07:01.910
How it feels to throw 
away your duelist pride!

00:07:01.910 --> 00:07:02.710
Jack-

00:07:02.710 --> 00:07:04.100
You don't know how it feels!

00:07:09.170 --> 00:07:11.910
I only wanted to cheer him up.

00:07:11.910 --> 00:07:14.850
Jack doesn't know how he's supposed to feel.

00:07:23.750 --> 00:07:26.730
Yusei, sorry about that.

00:07:27.020 --> 00:07:28.910
I shouldn't have yelled.

00:07:29.480 --> 00:07:31.420
Apologize to Rua for me.

00:07:31.550 --> 00:07:34.390
Don't worry about it.  Rua understands.

00:07:34.510 --> 00:07:37.030
I feel pathetic.

00:07:37.580 --> 00:07:40.770
I thought I was on top of the 
dueling world and proclaimed to be

00:07:40.770 --> 00:07:44.380
the King, but Godwin was playing 
me like a puppet the entire time.

00:07:44.830 --> 00:07:45.750
Jack...

00:07:46.260 --> 00:07:48.270
Don't blame yourself.

00:07:48.270 --> 00:07:50.950
Jack, you only wanted to attain power.

00:07:51.210 --> 00:07:54.710
But in reality, Godwin coaxed Dragan.

00:07:55.820 --> 00:08:02.600
My pride as a duelist won't forgive 
me for feeling good about beating him.

00:08:02.600 --> 00:08:05.320
Then prove it in tomorrow's duel.

00:08:06.320 --> 00:08:10.410
Who would've been the real 
winner - Dragan or Jack?

00:08:10.840 --> 00:08:12.670
Believe in your duelist pride.

00:08:15.840 --> 00:08:19.310
I'll be the real winner, of course!

00:08:26.680 --> 00:08:32.520
It's almost the finals of the 
first-ever WRGP tournament!

00:08:32.900 --> 00:08:37.260
In A Block, Team New World 
already made the finals.

00:08:37.260 --> 00:08:42.390
Who will win this duel and advance to 
the finals to battle Team New World?

00:08:42.390 --> 00:08:46.870
Will it be Jack Atlas and 
Yusei Fudo's Team 5D's?

00:08:46.870 --> 00:08:52.940
Or will it be Team Raganarok with 
their three god-powered Aesir Cards?

00:08:53.870 --> 00:08:57.360
Please let Jack win!

00:08:57.620 --> 00:09:00.820
I can't believe his semifinal 
opponent is Dragan.

00:09:00.820 --> 00:09:02.820
Destiny is ironic.

00:09:03.400 --> 00:09:07.850
If Jack loses, what'll he do 
to me to release his anger?

00:09:09.140 --> 00:09:10.060
Ahem.

00:09:12.000 --> 00:09:13.700
Step step step.

00:09:15.170 --> 00:09:18.300
You must win, Jack Atlas!

00:09:18.300 --> 00:09:20.900
You were once known as the King!

00:09:24.250 --> 00:09:26.380
It's finally time.

00:09:27.650 --> 00:09:28.930
Right, Dragan?

00:09:29.320 --> 00:09:31.210
Brave.  Harald.

00:09:31.570 --> 00:09:34.200
Yeah.  I thank you both.

00:09:34.580 --> 00:09:39.300
Brave, I recalled my fighting 
spirit because of you.

00:09:39.440 --> 00:09:47.140
If Harald didn't arrive back then, I'd still 
be hiding alone in that snowy mountain.

00:09:47.490 --> 00:09:49.600
I know how you feel.

00:09:50.050 --> 00:09:53.560
But for now, focus on defeating him 
and battle with all your strength.

00:09:53.900 --> 00:09:57.510
That will help Team Ragnarok.

00:10:00.400 --> 00:10:04.660
The first wheelers Jack and 
Dragan are at the starting line!

00:10:04.850 --> 00:10:07.910
The match is about to begin!

00:10:09.630 --> 00:10:11.020
Jack!

00:10:11.020 --> 00:10:12.670
Master Atlas!

00:10:12.830 --> 00:10:15.020
Is Jack okay?

00:10:15.200 --> 00:10:15.960
Yeah.

00:10:16.310 --> 00:10:17.750
Duel Mode on.

00:10:19.360 --> 00:10:21.160
Let's go, Jack Atlas!

00:10:21.580 --> 00:10:23.620
I'll defeat you this time!

00:10:24.140 --> 00:10:25.480
Bring it!

00:10:26.010 --> 00:10:28.670
Jack Atlas won't lose to the likes of you!

00:10:33.900 --> 00:10:38.790
I promise to get back my damaged pride.

00:10:40.760 --> 00:10:42.530
Riding Duel!

00:10:43.600 --> 00:10:45.030
Acceleration!

00:10:47.760 --> 00:10:49.610
Jack Atlas took the lead!

00:10:52.880 --> 00:10:54.730
His acceleration is incredible!

00:10:56.490 --> 00:10:59.760
So that's how passionate 
you are about this duel!

00:10:59.760 --> 00:11:01.140
But I won't lose!

00:11:02.600 --> 00:11:06.570
You won't defeat this vehicle 
that took us a year to build!

00:11:08.780 --> 00:11:13.200
Jack Atlas took the corner first!

00:11:14.800 --> 00:11:16.120
All right!  He goes first!

00:11:16.250 --> 00:11:16.950
Duel!

00:11:21.170 --> 00:11:23.450
What?  These cards...

00:11:23.760 --> 00:11:26.190
It's the same hand as before!

00:11:26.390 --> 00:11:29.190
Unbelievable!

00:11:47.080 --> 00:11:49.350
Is this actually happening?

00:11:49.900 --> 00:11:53.920
My hand is exactly the same as before.

00:11:54.970 --> 00:12:01.550
Is it coincidence, or is destiny 
recreating our previous battle?

00:12:02.200 --> 00:12:03.660
My turn!

00:12:05.260 --> 00:12:06.820
It's the same card as before!

00:12:07.620 --> 00:12:14.890
In order to restore my damaged pride, I must 
defeat that set card and win the previous duel.

00:12:16.340 --> 00:12:18.250
I summon Top Runner!

00:12:22.020 --> 00:12:24.580
Top Runner?  That's the same as before!

00:12:24.840 --> 00:12:27.740
I set two cards and end my turn!

00:12:28.500 --> 00:12:30.060
Now bring it, Dragan!

00:12:30.060 --> 00:12:34.260
It's our destiny to finish our previous duel!

00:12:34.850 --> 00:12:38.510
I see!  He also has the same cards as before!

00:12:39.300 --> 00:12:45.670
The goddess of destiny has given me 
this duel so that I can get my revenge!

00:12:47.300 --> 00:12:50.630
Let's battle, Jack Atlas!  My turn!

00:12:54.770 --> 00:12:57.330
I summon Garmr of the Nordic Beasts!

00:13:02.490 --> 00:13:05.500
Top Runner and Garmr of the Nordic Beasts.

00:13:05.650 --> 00:13:08.190
This is the exact same duel as before.

00:13:08.460 --> 00:13:14.270
Then I set one card and end my turn!

00:13:15.340 --> 00:13:16.220
There it is!

00:13:16.410 --> 00:13:17.670
My turn!

00:13:19.170 --> 00:13:21.480
I summon Power Breaker!

00:13:25.200 --> 00:13:29.990
Level 4 Top Runner tunes 
Level 4 Power Breaker!

00:13:29.990 --> 00:13:32.700
The pulse of the King now forms a line here!

00:13:32.700 --> 00:13:34.830
Witness the power of the rumbling heavens!

00:13:34.830 --> 00:13:36.350
Synchro Summon!

00:13:37.140 --> 00:13:39.950
My soul!  Red Dragon Archfiend!

00:13:39.950 --> 00:13:46.430
Jack Atlas successfully summoned his 
ace monster Red Dragon Archfiend!

00:13:48.280 --> 00:13:49.590
There's no mistake.

00:13:49.920 --> 00:13:54.050
Jack and Dragan are fighting 
the same duel as before.

00:13:54.050 --> 00:13:55.300
Same duel?

00:13:55.860 --> 00:13:58.050
So the set card is the same?

00:13:58.500 --> 00:14:00.790
Destiny does interesting things.

00:14:01.230 --> 00:14:02.710
Bring it, Dragan!

00:14:02.910 --> 00:14:04.460
I won't run or hide!

00:14:04.810 --> 00:14:08.610
Try to defeat me with that set card!

00:14:12.160 --> 00:14:16.460
Do you understand your agreement 
with Director Godwin?

00:14:18.460 --> 00:14:19.950
Here I go, Dragan!

00:14:20.230 --> 00:14:24.080
Red Dragon Archfiend attacks 
Garmr of the Nordic Beasts!

00:14:24.080 --> 00:14:26.910
Absolute Powerforce!

00:14:26.910 --> 00:14:28.010
I activate my trap!

00:14:28.480 --> 00:14:31.050
Nordic Relic Brisingamen!

00:14:31.220 --> 00:14:32.090
There it is!

00:14:32.090 --> 00:14:33.410
That's the card of destiny?

00:14:35.200 --> 00:14:39.350
You risked your pride with that 
card!  Show me its effect!

00:14:39.990 --> 00:14:43.780
My monster's attack points become the same as

00:14:43.780 --> 00:14:49.050
another monster's original attack 
points until the End Phase!

00:14:49.630 --> 00:14:52.360
I select Red Dragon Archfiend!

00:14:54.160 --> 00:14:57.510
It's like there are two 
Red Dragon Archfiends!

00:14:57.710 --> 00:15:02.300
When Garmr destroys your 
monster while it's powered up

00:15:02.300 --> 00:15:05.320
by this effect, you take damage 
equal to its attack points!

00:15:05.520 --> 00:15:06.270
What?

00:15:06.580 --> 00:15:12.760
If Red Dragon Archfiend is destroyed in this 
battle, Jack takes 3000 points of damage!

00:15:13.370 --> 00:15:15.940
So this is what Dragan's set card does!

00:15:16.180 --> 00:15:18.640
Interesting!  I'll take it on!

00:15:19.200 --> 00:15:20.160
Here I go, Dragan!

00:15:20.160 --> 00:15:23.810
Now begins the real battle 
where we wager our prides!

00:15:23.810 --> 00:15:26.660
I activate my Counter Trap Reaction Summon!

00:15:27.050 --> 00:15:30.870
When your monster's attack 
points change, I can

00:15:30.870 --> 00:15:35.140
Special Summon one Level 4-or-below 
monster from my graveyard!

00:15:35.320 --> 00:15:38.380
I Special Summon Top Runner!

00:15:38.520 --> 00:15:46.060
Due to Top Runner's effect, my Synchro 
Monster gains 600 attack points!

00:15:50.350 --> 00:15:52.240
3600 attack points!

00:15:52.240 --> 00:15:55.190
All right!  It has more attack 
points than the opponent!

00:15:55.190 --> 00:15:57.440
Go, Red Dragon Archfiend!

00:15:57.440 --> 00:16:00.180
Absolute Powerforce!

00:16:05.360 --> 00:16:08.640
He did it!  He defeated Dragan's trap card!

00:16:08.640 --> 00:16:11.020
The previous battle is over!

00:16:11.010 --> 00:16:15.650
Do you now know that you can't defeat me?

00:16:19.040 --> 00:16:21.170
Not good enough, Jack Atlas!

00:16:21.520 --> 00:16:24.630
I knew that Garmr would be destroyed.

00:16:24.630 --> 00:16:27.300
That trap is only the beginning!

00:16:27.530 --> 00:16:28.160
What?

00:16:28.500 --> 00:16:35.170
I can Special Summon this card from my hand 
when a monster on my field is destroyed in battle!

00:16:35.170 --> 00:16:39.040
I Special Summon Tanngnjostr of the 
Nordic Beasts in defense position!

00:16:43.730 --> 00:16:45.350
Bring it, Jack Atlas!

00:16:45.350 --> 00:16:47.450
The real battle is just getting started!

00:16:50.020 --> 00:16:53.060
The trap card wasn't his trump card.

00:16:53.420 --> 00:16:55.250
He's planning to summon a god.

00:16:55.250 --> 00:16:59.520
Jack Atlas completely fell 
for Dragan's strategy.

00:17:00.070 --> 00:17:03.270
He'll find out how dangerous a god really is.

00:17:03.750 --> 00:17:07.730
Top Runner attacks Tanngnjostr 
of the Nordic Beasts!

00:17:15.060 --> 00:17:17.610
Why did he attack when 
he couldn't destroy it?

00:17:17.980 --> 00:17:20.100
In order to protect Top Runner.

00:17:20.290 --> 00:17:23.750
During the End Phase, Red 
Dragon Archfiend's effect

00:17:23.750 --> 00:17:26.930
destroys all monsters on his 
own field that didn't attack.

00:17:26.930 --> 00:17:28.090
Oh yeah.

00:17:29.280 --> 00:17:32.400
I set one card and end my turn!

00:17:33.520 --> 00:17:34.690
My turn!

00:17:36.110 --> 00:17:40.720
I switch Tanngnjostr of the Nordic Beasts 
from defense position to attack position!

00:17:44.950 --> 00:17:48.170
When this card switches from 
defense to attack position, I can

00:17:48.170 --> 00:17:51.990
Special Summon one Tanngrisnir of 
the Nordic Beasts from my deck!

00:17:53.010 --> 00:17:55.930
Appear, Tanngrisnir of the Nordic Beasts!

00:17:59.680 --> 00:18:06.590
I can Special Summon this card from my hand 
when a Synchro Monster is on your field!

00:18:06.590 --> 00:18:09.790
I Special Summon the Tuner Monster Guldfaxe!

00:18:12.890 --> 00:18:14.240
Tuner Monster?

00:18:14.240 --> 00:18:15.420
Can it be?

00:18:15.670 --> 00:18:18.210
He's planning to summon 
Thor, Lord of the Aesir.

00:18:18.930 --> 00:18:20.040
I see.

00:18:20.520 --> 00:18:28.190
He let Jack destroy Garmr so that he 
could use the trap card to summon a god.

00:18:29.820 --> 00:18:31.900
Here I go, Jack Atlas!

00:18:32.710 --> 00:18:38.980
Level 4 Guldfaxe tunes Level 3 
Tanngrisnir and Level 3 Tanngnjostr!

00:18:39.860 --> 00:18:45.200
When the gate to the star world opens, the 
ancient god of battle swings its magical hammer.

00:18:46.120 --> 00:18:49.740
As the earth trembles, it 
arrives with roaring thunder!

00:18:50.740 --> 00:18:52.190
Synchro Summon!

00:18:53.030 --> 00:18:56.770
Come, Thor, Lord of the Aesir!

00:19:11.500 --> 00:19:13.450
It's here!

00:19:13.450 --> 00:19:15.960
Dragan's ace monster!

00:19:15.960 --> 00:19:22.730
It's Thor, Lord of the Aesir, one of the 
three Aesir Cards that have the power of the gods!

00:19:22.730 --> 00:19:24.790
What's that monster?

00:19:24.790 --> 00:19:26.780
It's like a real god.

00:19:26.970 --> 00:19:31.570
I heard stories about this monster, 
but I didn't know it actually existed.

00:19:31.920 --> 00:19:35.230
Thor, Lord of the Aesir has arrived.

00:19:35.990 --> 00:19:38.980
The three Aesir have finally appeared!

00:19:39.680 --> 00:19:43.140
But Thor, Lord of the Aesir 
has 3500 attack points.

00:19:43.480 --> 00:19:48.470
Due to Top Runner's effect, Red Dragon 
Archfiend has 3600 attack points.

00:19:48.470 --> 00:19:52.160
Thor, Lord of the Aesir can't 
destroy Red Dragon Archfiend!

00:19:52.390 --> 00:19:54.510
You still don't understand.

00:19:54.870 --> 00:19:57.790
I'll show you the power of a god!

00:19:57.790 --> 00:20:00.480
Thor, Lord of the Aesir's effect activates!

00:20:00.890 --> 00:20:07.540
Once per turn, this card negates 
and gains your monster's effect!

00:20:07.680 --> 00:20:08.420
What?

00:20:08.990 --> 00:20:13.080
I negate Top Runner's effect, 
and then I use that effect

00:20:13.080 --> 00:20:16.520
to increase Thor, Lord of the 
Aesir's attack points by 600!

00:20:16.530 --> 00:20:18.750
Effect Absorber!

00:20:26.980 --> 00:20:28.940
4100 attack points?

00:20:29.520 --> 00:20:34.050
Jack kept Top Runner because 
he anticipated that Dragan

00:20:34.050 --> 00:20:38.320
would summon Thor, but that 
